      "widgets_values": [
        "Krea 2 V10 reference workflow\n\nThis workflow shows the Krea reference route:\nLoad Image -> KG Krea 2 Image Guide Card V10 -> KG Krea 2 Reference Stack Encoder V10 -> sampler positive input.\n\nEverything from the V9 starter workflow still applies; V10 adds:\n- Four more quick recipes: suggest the color palette, use the background/setting, copy the camera framing, and mood board only.\n- Guide direction: away from this image turns a card into a counter-example (see krea-v10-counter-example-workflow.json).\n- When this card guides: per-card timing (whole image, early layout only, final details only).\n- Balance strong cards: keeps several hot cards from fighting. off - use my values is exact V9 behavior.\n- Reuse image studies: re-runs that change only strengths/timing/balance skip every encoder pass. Watch the Studies line in the stack report.\n- stack_report output: wired to the Preview Any node on the right. It explains what every card requested, what it actually got, and why (feel curve, recipe cap, text/logo guard).\n- prepared_references output: wired to the Preview Image node on the right. It shows exactly what the vision encoder studied after treatments.\n\nWhat to edit first:\n1. Write the desired final image in the V10 stack prompt, or leave it blank when the cards fully describe the job.\n2. Put your reference images into the Load Image nodes.\n3. On each Guide Card V10, choose Use image for.\n4. Start with low image strengths and raise slowly - then read the stack report to see the effective values.\n5. Leave the model, sampler, negative prompt, and Save Image wiring alone unless you intentionally want to change the demo graph.\n\nStarting strength values:\n- 0.00 means off.\n- 0.03 to 0.08 is a tiny nudge.\n- 0.10 to 0.25 is gentle guidance.\n- 0.25 to 0.45 is strong guidance.\n- Above 0.50 can overpower weak prompts unless the card is a content anchor.\n\nText/logo safety:\nUse avoid copying text/logos when the reference contains words, labels, logos, UI, screenshots, symbols, or brand marks. Keep its strength around 0.03 to 0.05.\n\nLearn more:\n- docs/krea-v10-documentation-index.md\n- docs/nodes/kg-krea-2-image-guide-card-v10.md\n- docs/nodes/kg-krea-2-reference-stack-encoder-v10.md\n- example_workflows/krea-v10-full-showcase-workflow.json\n- example_workflows/krea-v10-counter-example-workflow.json\n"
      ],
      "title": "How to use this Krea V10 reference stack workflow",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
